This file contains upgrading tools/scripts/...

Usually you should stop whole BBS and then run scripts here.

With nest.svc (CONFIG_NEST_SVC), the files of the boards (.DIR, articles)
are only its cache, and .BRD is mirrored into it. These tools write the
files directly, not through BoF, so:

 - Run the tools that rewrite posts or .DIR (convert_utf8, convert_sgr_66,
   fix_2026h, dir_recommend_to_rating) before the boards are imported into
   nest.svc (`nest.ctl import-board`); on a site already on nest.svc, the
   next render or sync of nest.svc reverts them. Stop nest.svc, run them,
   and import the boards again.
 - After the tools that rewrite .BRD (board_split_title,
   migrate_board_moderators), run `nest.ctl import-boards`.

See docs/nest_migration.md.
